  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Bowery Ballroom in New York on March 28, 2011, presenting a 24-song set that captured a significant moment in their catalog [1][2]. The recommended recording, uploaded by nyctaper, is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, offering a balanced audio perspective of the 105-minute show [1]. The lineup featured John Darnielle on vocals and guitar, Peter Hughes on bass and vocals, Jon Wurster on drums, and Yuval Semo on keyboards and guitar, with Craig Finn joining for some tracks [2]. This performance is notable for including several songs appearing in the archive for the first time, such as “Estate Sale Sign,” “High Hawk Season,” “You Were Cool,” “Outer Scorpion Squadron,” “Prowl Great Cain,” and “Plain” [1]. It also featured rare “bustout” tracks like “Seeing Daylight,” which had not been played in over nine years, and “Family Happiness,” a song absent from the stage for nearly thirteen years [1]. A separate audience recording by Bluesmer, rated five stars by one listener, is also available; that reviewer praised the steady audio quality and the setlist, noting it was a top-three favorite bootleg [2][3]. While the recommended file documents its lineage clearly, the alternative recording provides a different vantage point from the crowd [1][2]. The show concluded with a four-song encore, including “Baboon” and “No Children,” rounding out a comprehensive capture of the evening [1].",
